(459254, 42883, 7599, '<td valign="top">Very soft image with the sunset background, but the subject itself pops out. I like the negative space, but I''m still having an inner debate whether or not I would have changed the orientation and rearranged the negative space to add more upwards, while removing from the left. Given that the image is so straight and has a natural upwards motion, as well as the majority of the suns colours being really centralized I think I would have flipped to portrait. But that''s just my opinion. I still really like the shot as presented.</td>', 'Very soft image with the sunset background, but the subject itself pops out. I like the negative space, but I''m still having an inner debate whether or not I would have changed the orientation and rearranged the negative space to add more upwards, while removing from the left. Given that the image is so straight and has a natural upwards motion, as well as the majority of the suns colours being really centralized I think I would have flipped to portrait. But that''s just my opinion. I still really like the shot as presented.', '2003-10-22 20:51:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(459255, 43414, 3102, '<td valign="top">That''s quite a unique location!</td>', 'That''s quite a unique location!', '2003-10-22 20:52:22.000000', NULL, 1),
