(465666, 43409, 1280, '<td valign="top">I sincerely thank each of you who commented.  A couple of bad things happened to me last week.  My computer gave up the ghost completely, and the old laptop I''m borrowing didn''t show how terrible this turned out.  The other thing is I''m having intermittent problems with my camera and had to go back to using my first digicam I bought as my product camera on eBay years ago.  It''s not even a full mp.  It''s just 640 X 480, with no room for cropping etc.  <br/>I prolly just shouldn''t have entered, but old habits die hard.<br/>Thanks everyone for commenting.  I really appreciate the honesty.<br/></td>', 'I sincerely thank each of you who commented.  A couple of bad things happened to me last week.  My computer gave up the ghost completely, and the old laptop I''m borrowing didn''t show how terrible this turned out.  The other thing is I''m having intermittent problems with my camera and had to go back to using my first digicam I bought as my product camera on eBay years ago.  It''s not even a full mp.  It''s just 640 X 480, with no room for cropping etc.  I prolly just shouldn''t have entered, but old habits die hard.Thanks everyone for commenting.  I really appreciate the honesty.', '2003-10-29 09:39:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(465677, 42589, 12654, '<td valign="top">dear dudes and dudettes,<br/>I have no idea why this pic is dark on ur screens, it looks fine on mine.<br/>I have a Packard Bell monitor - yes its old - but its brightess and contrast is excellent, much better than most of the new monitors , my friends have.<br/>Oh well i dunno - but i do see the other pics well too.<br/>Anyhoo - i used a high ISO (400) to get the grainy effect as a coolness factor - well i guess it wasnt appreciated by many.<br/>Well what i thought of today was if i had turned off all the lights and got a atble lamp and focused it on my roomie - it would have tured out better - may be next time.<br/> <br/></td>', 'dear dudes and dudettes,I have no idea why this pic is dark on ur screens, it looks fine on mine.I have a Packard Bell monitor - yes its old - but its brightess and contrast is excellent, much better than most of the new monitors , my friends have.Oh well i dunno - but i do see the other pics well too.Anyhoo - i used a high ISO (400) to get the grainy effect as a coolness factor - well i guess it wasnt appreciated by many.Well what i thought of today was if i had turned off all the lights and got a atble lamp and focused it on my roomie - it would have tured out better - may be next time. ', '2003-10-29 09:46:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(465682, 43416, 3540, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/>By Inspzil<br/> <br/>Composition - I think your idea is good.  I would''ve like to have seen the back 2 marble a little more on an even horizon (for lack of a better word).  The framing of the image makes me uncomfortable (again for lack of a better word) in that I don''t feel that its balanced.  Of course the front marble is the big focus point, so it should be closer and nicely focused, just maybe not quite so close and/or the back marbles could''ve been just a little closer.  I think it would have been just as effective if they were a little more in focus.<br/> <br/>Technical - I think you pretty much have it.  Very very well taken.<br/> <br/>Overall - The personification of marbles is a little difficult to deal with and stir any strong emotions in people to compel them to give you a great score.  I think everyone who voted probably was capable of seeing what the point of this photo was.  It just doesn''t translate well from people to glass.  There is one thought I had about the lighting in this photo, not to say that it''s done poorly by any means.  But that was to shorten the exposure somewhat and adding a little light to the 2 marbles only, to give a little more lighting induced mood.  That might be completely preposterous, but it''s just a thought I figured I could wing it out here and you can laugh at it or just ignore it as needed.  Best of luck in the challenges ahead - Bob</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique ClubBy Inspzil Composition - I think your idea is good.  I would''ve like to have seen the back 2 marble a little more on an even horizon (for lack of a better word).  The framing of the image makes me uncomfortable (again for lack of a better word) in that I don''t feel that its balanced.  Of course the front marble is the big focus point, so it should be closer and nicely focused, just maybe not quite so close and/or the back marbles could''ve been just a little closer.  I think it would have been just as effective if they were a little more in focus. Technical - I think you pretty much have it.  Very very well taken. Overall - The personification of marbles is a little difficult to deal with and stir any strong emotions in people to compel them to give you a great score.  I think everyone who voted probably was capable of seeing what the point of this photo was.  It just doesn''t translate well from people to glass.  There is one thought I had about the lighting in this photo, not to say that it''s done poorly by any means.  But that was to shorten the exposure somewhat and adding a little light to the 2 marbles only, to give a little more lighting induced mood.  That might be completely preposterous, but it''s just a thought I figured I could wing it out here and you can laugh at it or just ignore it as needed.  Best of luck in the challenges ahead - Bob', '2003-10-29 09:51:10.000000', NULL, 0),
