(467631, 42935, 10625, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BobsterLobster:</b></div><hr/><i>For me, the most underrated picture this challenge. Great composition... I''m not normally a fan of centred subjects, but it works well here. The shot is perhaps a little oversaturated and oversharpened, but it''s a great Autumn picture. I was going to add this to my favourites, but I notice you haven''t been too generous with your ''helpful'' ticks on the comments below so I think I''ll add another shot instead. I do feel that many people deserve a tick who put time and effort into giving you a perfectly helpful and reasonable comment.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Bobster, i too think that people deserve to know when their comment was helpful but we all have a different idea of what "helpful" is.  Telling someone they have nice colours is good and well, but as a learner, I think that a little depth to the comment may have helped me to think of other ways to improve.  it''s not that i don''t appreciate their comment, i do, but that may not be my idea of what is "helpful". i too was disappointed at the results of this photo only because i was quite happy with what it said to me.  thanks for your comment.</td>', 'Originally posted by BobsterLobster:For me, the most underrated picture this challenge. Great composition... I''m not normally a fan of centred subjects, but it works well here. The shot is perhaps a little oversaturated and oversharpened, but it''s a great Autumn picture. I was going to add this to my favourites, but I notice you haven''t been too generous with your ''helpful'' ticks on the comments below so I think I''ll add another shot instead. I do feel that many people deserve a tick who put time and effort into giving you a perfectly helpful and reasonable comment.  Bobster, i too think that people deserve to know when their comment was helpful but we all have a different idea of what "helpful" is.  Telling someone they have nice colours is good and well, but as a learner, I think that a little depth to the comment may have helped me to think of other ways to improve.  it''s not that i don''t appreciate their comment, i do, but that may not be my idea of what is "helpful". i too was disappointed at the results of this photo only because i was quite happy with what it said to me.  thanks for your comment.', '2003-10-30 19:32:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(467708, 43038, 10985, '<td valign="top">This is one sweet cat shot. It has a lot of emotive weight to it and the fact that the kitten is not facing the camera/viewer gives it more impact, in my opinion. The light is very interesting, too, althought there are a few burnt spots.</td>', 'This is one sweet cat shot. It has a lot of emotive weight to it and the fact that the kitten is not facing the camera/viewer gives it more impact, in my opinion. The light is very interesting, too, althought there are a few burnt spots.', '2003-10-30 21:10:06.000000', NULL, 0),
